- Story & Context: Quarantined inside the vessel's decompression pod in Tema Harbour, Kofi spent fourteen days tapping out syncopated palm-wine counter-melodies on the chamber's steel bulkheads with a rusted wrench. The sound of his sisters harmonizing through the habitat's life-support radio drove the ship's night watchmen into panicked insomnia, unable to distinguish the music from structural metal fatigue. As condensation dripped into his open acoustic guitar soundhole, he confessed his descent into nitrogen narcosis through the glass porthole, whispering: "I traded daylight for twenty fathoms of singing glass."
